      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/mnlstandardph/status/1958427955782381853",
      "text": "IN PHOTOS | Philippine Army soldiers and their Australian counterparts are strengthening their interoperability through joint training under Exercise Amphibious Landing Operations (Exercise ALON) 2025, which runs from August 11 to 29 in Nueva Ecija.\n\nTroops from the Army’s 84th Infantry “Victorious” Battalion of the 7th Infantry “Kaugnay” Division are participating in land warfare exercises at Fort Magsaysay and other training areas. Their training includes combat shooting, jungle operations, live-fire exercises, and urban combat supported by armor, artillery, and engineering units.\n\nMore than 3,600 personnel from the Philippines, Australia, the United States, and Canada are taking part in Exercise ALON, which also features amphibious landings, air-sea operations, and joint maneuvers. Japan, South Korea, New Zealand, and Indonesia are observing the exercises as part of broader regional defense cooperation. | via Rex Espiritu\n\nFor more info, visit https://t.co/rmQCnNSOvI.",
