    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1958437450868834449",
      "url": "https://x.com/mnlstandardph/status/1958437450868834449",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/mnlstandardph/status/1958437450868834449",
      "text": "IN PHOTOS | Ongoing flood-control works continue in Binondo, Manila, despite President Ferdinand Marcos Jr.’s recent disclosure of anomalies in several projects. \n\nMayor Isko Moreno reminded the Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) and the Metropolitan Manila Development Authority (MMDA) on Thursday (August 21) to secure permits from the city government before undertaking such infrastructure works, stressing that all projects must align with Manila’s City Drainage Master Plan to prevent flooding and ensure accountability.\n\n📷 Norman Cruz\n\nFor more info, visit https://t.co/rmQCnNSOvI.",
